# MQ03 "Find the Heir" and MS48 "Breaking the Siege of Kvatch". MQ02 50 started MQ03 (10): Martin is a priest at
# Kvatch. Savlian Matius (camp outside the ruined city) says Martin led survivors to the Chapel of Akatosh (MQ03 40)
# and asks for help closing the Oblivion Gate (MS48 10). Inside the Gate, Ilend Vonius (20) points the way to the
# captured Menien Goneld in a small tower (30); the Sigil Keeper's key opens the Sigil Keep (40); taking the Sigil
# Stone closes the Gate (50). Savlian then leads the attack on the plaza (60 -> 80), the chapel is freed (90, 100),
# and Martin agrees to come to Weynon Priory (MQ03 50 -> 60, which starts MQ04).
# The ride to Kvatch is the player's travel: `approach` Savlian stands in for it (no follower is along).

# Savlian's first greeting "Stand back, civilian!" (INFO 00024853, say once) sets MS48 5 and offers "What happened
# here?" / "What will you do now?". "Martin" (INFO 0001E8AA, Savlian) sets MQ03 40; "Help" sets MS48 8 and offers
# "I'll do whatever I can.", which sets MS48 10.
# He force-greets (package MS48SavlianMatiusGreetPlayer, MS48 < 5). Until run 18a the greeting was spoken before
# the Dialogue Menu opened and its two questions were never offered (runs 4h, 5j); since the say-once greetings
# keep their choices until one is answered (TES4SaidOnce_<fid>), the menu lists exactly those two. "What happened
# here?" (INFO 00098142) offers "What will you do now?" (INFO 00098143), which returns to his topics.
case mq03_savlian
expect GetStageDone MQ03 10
approach SavlianMatiusRef
hear 300 SavlianMatiusRef Stand back, civilian
hear 300 SavlianMatiusRef Get back to the encampment
until 300 GetStageDone MS48 5
wait 30
ask "What happened here?"
ask "What will you do now?"
until 300 MS48.donowchoice == 1
ask "Martin"
until 300 GetStageDone MQ03 40
ask "Help"
until 300 GetStageDone MS48 8
ask "I'll do whatever I can."
until 300 GetStageDone MS48 10
bye
end

# The player goes through the Gate (MS48KvatchGate, a load door into the Oblivion plane) and finds Ilend Vonius. His
# greeting offers "It's all right. What's going on?" (MS48 20); "Fine. Captain Matius needs your help." sends him back
# alone (the other answer, MS48 25, takes him along as a follower).
# Ilend is fighting when the player comes through; a player joins in. `defend IlendVoniusRef` has the player kill
# whatever attacks them or Ilend (run 18b: the player stood by in god mode and Ilend was dead when the case
# reached him; 19a: defending only the player was too late for him).
case ms48_gate_ilend
defend IlendVoniusRef
activate MS48KvatchGate
wait 60
approach IlendVoniusRef
talk IlendVoniusRef
ask "It's all right. What's going on?"
until 300 GetStageDone MS48 20
ask "Fine. Captain Matius needs your help."
bye
end

# Menien Goneld, caged at the top of the small tower (OblivionMqKvatchSmallTower01), greets the player: "Quickly,
# quickly! There's no time!" (MS48 30): the Sigil Keeper's key opens the great tower.
# The Sigil Keeper guards the cage and attacks on sight; while he fights, a `talk` to Menien only gets the greeting
# spoken aloud with no conversation (4i), and without a `talk` he only calls for help (4j). A player kills the
# Keeper first: kill stands in for that fight, then the player talks to Menien. His greeting is a monologue that
# opens no menu and comes only once his cries for help have stopped (4l: 90 ticks after the activation), so the
# case activates him and waits for the stage, not for a conversation.
case ms48_menien
approach MenienGoneldRef01
run
MS48DremoraSigilKeeperRef.kill
wait 90
activate MenienGoneldRef01
until 900 GetStageDone MS48 30
bye if open
end

# The Sigil Keeper (MS48DremoraSigilKeeperRef, in OblivionMqKvatchSmallTower01) carries the key; taking it from his
# body sets 40 (MS48OblivionSigilKeySCRIPT OnAdd, MS48 >= 30). He is already dead (ms48_menien); RemoveAllItems
# stands in for looting the body.
case ms48_sigil_key
run
player.moveto MS48DremoraSigilKeeperRef
wait 60
run
MS48DremoraSigilKeeperRef.RemoveAllItems player
until 300 GetStageDone MS48 40
end

# The Sigil Stone (SigilStoneMS48, top of the Sigil Keep) closes the Gate: taking it puts the player back in Tamriel
# beside the destroyed Gate, whose script sets 50 (MS48OblivionGateScript: GetDestroyed, MS48 < 50). The quest then
# waits for the player to report to Savlian.
case ms48_sigil_stone
run
player.moveto SigilStoneMS48
wait 60
activate SigilStoneMS48
until 1800 GetStageDone MS48 50
end

# Savlian's greeting after the Gate offers "I'm ready. Let's go." (INFO 0001E8AC: "For Kvatch!", 60). He leads the
# guards to the southern plaza (65, his travel's OnPackageDone); the plaza creatures' OnLoad sets 70 at 60, as does
# his "Follow me! For Kvatch!" greeting. moveto his plaza mark stands in for following him.
case ms48_plaza
approach SavlianMatiusRef
talk SavlianMatiusRef
ask "I'm ready. Let's go."
until 300 GetStageDone MS48 60
bye if open
run
player.moveto MS48SPos1Mark
until 900 GetStageDone MS48 70
end

# The six plaza creatures (MS48PlazaCreatureFinalScript each count a death; the sixth sets 80) are the leveled refs
# under enable parent 0007214A. kill stands in for the battle, all six in the same instant on purpose: each
# creature's own script adds 1 to MS48.monsterskilled, which used to lose a count when several added at once (run
# 6a: 80 never came). The converter now routes such adds through the owning script (TES4Add_<var>).
# Savlian's stage-80 greeting ("Ha ha! We wiped the bastards out!", INFO 00024851) sets 90. It is a goodbye: spoken, with no conversation left open for `talk` to
# find (run 4q), so the case activates him and waits for the stage.
case ms48_plaza_battle
run
0007200C.kill
0007200D.kill
0007200E.kill
0007200F.kill
00072010.kill
00072012.kill
until 900 GetStageDone MS48 80
approach SavlianMatiusRef
activate SavlianMatiusRef
until 600 GetStageDone MS48 90
bye if open
end

# Savlian leads the way into the Chapel of Akatosh (KvatchChapelofAkatosh); his greeting there (INFO 00028865, MS48 >=
# 80, GetInCell the chapel) sets 100, which ends MS48 and starts MS49. Martin's greeting offers three openings; "The
# Emperor told me to find you." leads, choice by choice, to "Come with me to Weynon Priory." (INFO 0001E8D7,
# MQ03 < 50), which sets MQ03 50. The plaza door was not loaded from where the battle left the player
# (run 4r), so moveto Savlian stands in for following him inside.
case ms48_chapel_martin
until 1800 SavlianMatiusRef.GetInCell KvatchChapelofAkatosh
run
player.moveto SavlianMatiusRef
wait 120
approach SavlianMatiusRef
activate SavlianMatiusRef
until 900 GetStageDone MS48 100
bye if open
# From MS48 95 Martin walks to the refugee camp (MS48RefugeesAtCamp, Wander r1200 at KvatchEncampmentMarker;
# run 38a: he left the chapel before the talk). The player meets him there.
until 7200 MartinRef.GetDistance KvatchEncampmentMarker < 1200
run
player.moveto MartinRef
wait 120
approach MartinRef
until 900 GetGlobalValue TES4DialogueOpen == 0
talk MartinRef
ask "The Emperor told me to find you."
ask "You're Martin, right? The priest?"
ask "There is a plan. We're part of it."
ask "You are Uriel Septim's son."
ask "The Emperor knew you were in danger."
ask "Why would I lie to you?"
ask "Come with me to Weynon Priory."
until 300 GetStageDone MQ03 50
bye if open
end
